This directory contains a technical report describing unravel
and the unravel source code developed at NIST.

This directory contains the following files and subdirectories:

FILES:
NIST-IR-5691-Volume-1.ps (Software design of unravel)
NIST-IR-5691-Volume-2.ps (user manual for unravel)
README	(this file)
vol1.ps.Z (NIST-IR-5691-Volume-1.ps in compressed form)
vol2.ps.Z (NIST-IR-5691-Volume-2.ps in compressed form)
src2.2+.tar.Z (The source file in compressed tar format)

SUBDIRECTORIES:
archive (older versions of unravel)
papers (Published papers about unravel)

To uncompress and untar the src type the following:

zcat src2.2+.tar.Z | tar xvf -

The subdirectory "archive/2.2-/" contains an earlier version.
Version 2.2+ contains some minor bug fixes that show up for
users of the "bash" shell and for users of gnu make.

We are interested in feedback on unravel.  We are planning another
release later this year that will include lifting some restrictions
(e.g., including goto statements in slices), tolerance for some
non-ANSI features and improving performance.

If you find unravel interesting or useful please let us know what you
like or find useful.  If you find bugs or have comments about the
tool's limitations let us know that too.

If you have problems or questions installing unravel I'll try to help
if you call (301) 975-3270 or send e-mail jlyle@nist.gov.

Dr. James R. Lyle
Information Technology Lab
